2.1. Overview of the production setup and the requirements for automation and control
To provide an overview of a production setup and to transition to the model development process, an overview of all the state variables, inputs, and disturbances or external resources are listed in Table 2. A typical production setup, as illustrated in Fig. 1, consists of several growing trays filled with substrate made of feed and water and populated with young larvae neonates. The growing trays consisting of the substrate and the larvae are referred to as growing medium. The environment where the growing mediums are placed are referred to as production environment in this work. The environment where the production setup is located and the resources are sourced is referred to as external or outside environment. The production environment may be completely closed, partially closed, or fully open. In a completely closed setup, as in case of complex closed bioreactors, all the resources (air, heat, humidity, water) to the production environment are supplied from external sources or generated using actuators. Such closed production setup can be described as
